{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"37a9f2d2a1fced82c495f07275d7b9ba377c12b03df1f3ce4fca3ed0eb1ced09","digest":{"component_or_area":"Backend port exception contract (Jira reconciler)","key_entities":["BackendHTTPError","urllib.error.HTTPError","jira.exceptions.JIRAError","_backend.py","jira_datacenter/transport.py","dispatch_apply_phases.py:119","outbound_differ.py:138-141","_safe_get_issue","_update_one_apply_reporter","_with_connection_retry"],"problem_keywords":["exception contract","transport abstraction","vendor coupling","jiraerror handling","deletion detection","http error mapping"],"propositions":["The DC transport raises JIRAError but core reconciler modules catch only urllib.error.HTTPError, causing exceptions to escape unhandled and degradation to fail","Deletion detection in outbound_differ._safe_get_issue silently breaks on DC because JIRAError is not caught and mapped to _DELETED like HTTPError 404","BackendHTTPError must be declared as the neutral exception contract on the port, subclassing urllib.error.HTTPError to preserve .code and require no core edits","DC transport must translate JIRAError to BackendHTTPError at the adapter boundary to prevent vendor exception types from leaking into core modules","The subclass relationship ensures existing catch clauses in core modules handle the translated exception and status code classification works identically for both Cloud and DC"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787750590020617001,"uuid":"b906dfd5-58d4-4f1a-b6dd-141b07f3be23"}